  "term": "Symptom Checklist-90–Revised",
  "definition": "The Symptom Checklist-90–Revised is a self-report questionnaire used to measure symptomatic distress. It covers 90 symptoms across nine problem areas and is widely used in general population and clinical research, with shorter versions available for briefer screening.",
